  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A school is organizing a trip to a theme park. The trip is offered to at least $12$ kids, and it can be attended by at most $20$ kids. The cost of each ticket is $$80$ if there are exactly $12$ kids. If there are more than $12$ kids, the price per ticket drops by $$4$ for each kid in excess of $12.$ Every kid pays the same amount for going on the trip.\n\nHow many kids must go on the trip for the theme park to maximize its revenue?",
